<!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
     SLIDE 2 — SECTION DIVIDER: NEUROIMAGING
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
<div class="slide slide-section" data-toc="Section 1: Neuroimaging &amp; Neurophysiology">
  <div class="section-center">
    <div class="section-num">01</div>
    <div class="section-title">Neuroimaging &amp; Neurophysiology</div>
    <div class="section-sub">MRI · CT · Amyloid/Tau PET · SPECT · EEG · Evoked Potentials</div>
    <p style="max-width:560px;color:#a8d8ea;margin-top:12px;">
      Biomarker-based diagnosis is now central to dementia classification. The 2024 revised Alzheimer's Association Research Framework (Jack et al., <em>Alzheimers Dement</em> 2024) and NIA-AA 2011 criteria anchor diagnosis to imaging and CSF/plasma biomarkers.
    </p>
