     SLIDE 19 — AI IN NEUROIMAGING ANALYSIS
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
<div class="slide slide-ai" data-toc="AI: Neuroimaging Analysis">
  <h2>AI in Neuroimaging — Automated Detection</h2>
  <div class="cards cards-2">
    <div class="card card-ai">
      <h3>MRI Volumetry &amp; Segmentation <span class="badge badge-ai">Deep Learning</span></h3>
      <ul class="bullet">
        <li><strong>3D CNNs</strong> (e.g., VGGNet, ResNet variants) trained on ADNI data achieve AUC 0.92–0.96 for AD vs. CN classification from structural MRI alone</li>
        <li>Automated hippocampal segmentation (FreeSurfer, FastSurfer) enables population-level normative modelling</li>
        <li><strong>SynthSeg</strong> (Billot et al., <em>NeuroImage</em> 2023): contrast-agnostic DL segmentation robust to MRI artefacts across scanners</li>
        <li>Detected hippocampal volume below age-norm predicts MCI→AD conversion (AUC 0.80) at 3 yrs</li>
      </ul>
      <span class="cite">Wen et al., Med Image Anal 2020; Billot et al., NeuroImage 2023</span>
    </div>
    <div class="card card-ai">
      <h3>Amyloid/Tau PET Analysis <span class="badge badge-ai">AI</span></h3>
      <ul class="bullet">
        <li>Deep learning SUVR quantification matches expert visual read with AUC &gt;0.97 (Klyuzhin et al., <em>J Nucl Med</em> 2022)</li>
        <li><strong>Early amyloid detection</strong>: DL models detect subtle amyloid PET positivity before visual threshold — potential for earlier intervention</li>
        <li>Tau staging models correlate with Braak stage (R² 0.85) using flortaucipir PET</li>
        <li>Multi-tracer models: joint amyloid+tau PET DL improves staging accuracy vs. single tracer</li>
      </ul>
      <span class="cite">Klyuzhin et al., J Nucl Med 2022; Ossenkoppele et al., Alzheimers Dement 2021</span>
    </div>
    <div class="card card-ai">
      <h3>Multi-Modal Fusion Models</h3>
      <ul class="bullet">
        <li>MRI + FDG-PET fusion: AUC 0.96 for AD classification (Liu et al., <em>Neuroimage</em> 2020)</li>
        <li>Multi-modal CNN + genetics (APOE ε4): improves MCI→AD prediction by 8–12% over imaging alone</li>
        <li><strong>Graph Neural Networks (GNNs)</strong>: model connectome disruption from rs-fMRI; detect AD network signatures</li>
        <li>Transformer models (e.g., BrainViT): self-supervised pretraining on 3D MRI; strong transfer learning for small dementia datasets</li>
      </ul>
      <span class="cite">Liu et al., Neuroimage 2020; Kawahara et al., Neuroimage 2017</span>
    </div>
    <div class="card card-ai">
      <h3>EEG-AI Dementia Biomarkers <span class="badge badge-new">Emerging</span></h3>
      <ul class="bullet">
        <li>CNN on resting EEG spectral features: 88% accuracy separating AD from healthy controls (Ieracitano et al., <em>Neural Netw</em> 2019)</li>
        <li>Graph Convolutional Networks on EEG coherence matrices detect AD connectivity signatures</li>
        <li>P300 latency + amplitude AI models: automated dementia screening tool (promising for low-resource settings)</li>
        <li>DL on ambulatory EEG: feasibility study for community screening</li>
      </ul>
      <span class="cite">Ieracitano et al., Neural Netw 2019; Babiloni et al., Clin Neurophysiol 2020</span>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

