<div class="slide slide-ai" data-toc="AI Ethics &amp; Governance">
  <h2>AI Ethics, Governance &amp; Equity in Dementia</h2>
  <div class="cards cards-2">
    <div class="card">
      <h3>Key Ethical Concerns</h3>
      <ul class="bullet">
        <li><strong>Bias &amp; equity</strong>: most AI training datasets (ADNI, UK Biobank) underrepresent Black, Hispanic, and Asian populations — models may perform worse in minority groups</li>
        <li><strong>Data privacy</strong>: neuroimaging, EHR, genomic data require GDPR/HIPAA-compliant federated learning or differential privacy</li>
        <li><strong>Informed consent</strong>: implications of early/predictive AI diagnosis (financial, insurance, psychological impact)</li>
        <li><strong>Autonomy</strong>: AI in care robots must respect person-centred dementia care principles</li>
      </ul>
      <span class="cite">WHO Ethics &amp; Governance of AI for Health 2021; Obermeyer et al., Science 2019</span>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <h3>Regulatory Landscape</h3>
      <ul class="bullet">
        <li>FDA 510(k) / De Novo pathway for AI/ML-based medical devices; >500 AI/ML devices cleared by 2024</li>
        <li>EU AI Act (2024): dementia diagnosis AI classified as high-risk — requires conformity assessment</li>
        <li>NHS AI Lab: NHSX AI in imaging programme — including dementia imaging AI deployment trials</li>
        <li>Alzheimer's Association AI Working Group: transparency and reproducibility standards for AD AI tools</li>
      </ul>
      <span class="cite">FDA AI/ML Action Plan 2021; EU AI Act 2024</span>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="warn-box" style="margin-top:14px;">
    <strong>Fairness Imperative:</strong> Dementia disproportionately affects women (60–65% of cases) and racialised minorities (2× higher risk in Black Americans). AI tools must be co-developed and validated in demographically representative cohorts to avoid exacerbating health inequities.
    <span class="cite">Alzheimer's Association Facts &amp; Figures 2024; Mayeda et al., Neurology 2016</span>
  </div>
</div>

